#: ../../source/docs/ground-effect-compensation.rst:5
#: 2f2fa5648b00451da5cd155638ade1ae
msgid "Ground Effect Compensation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ground-effect-compensation.rst:7
#: 07bd573202394be2a5cc43c5ff48e099
msgid ""
"Copter includes ground effect compensation which reduces the weighting of"
" the barometer (in favour of the accelerometers) when the vehicle is "
"likely taking off or landing.  This reduces the bounce sometimes seen "
"when landing vehicles with short legs compared to the length of their "
"propellers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ground-effect-compensation.rst:9
#: 91ed1e5db4594ee7a846106672b9ffed
msgid ""
"If your vehicle is not suffering from the bounce on landing it's best to "
"leave this feature disabled because it slightly increases the risk of "
"high vibration levels upsetting the altitude estimate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ground-effect-compensation.rst:12
#: e8a340c8b0414ec69e4c626514997353
msgid "Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ground-effect-compensation.rst:14
#: a1e5d7fbe9f64d6eb5ca606f3ab2524c
msgid ""
"Connect to the autopilot using your ground station (i.e. Mission Planner)"
" and set the :ref:`GND_EFFECT_COMP <GND_EFFECT_COMP>` parameter to \"1\"."
msgstr ""

